@ref Annex 2 B (src 965-967)
GIVEN `the annualised premium at issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Annex 2 B — the most that may be topped up in a policy year, the annualised premium at issue being` `the annualised premium at issue` MEANS
    10 TIMES `the annualised premium at issue`

@ref Annex 2 B (src 956-967, 974-975); Annex 2 C (src 987-991)
GIVEN `the request` IS A `A top-up request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Annex 2 B — the top-up is accepted:` `the request` MEANS
        `the request`'s `in writing on the Company's form`
    ... `the request`'s `every regular basic premium due has been paid`
    ... `the request`'s `every premium debt has been paid`
    ... `the request`'s `amount` AT LEAST `the request`'s `minimum top-up`
    ... `the request`'s `top-ups already paid in the policy year` PLUS `the request`'s `amount`
            AT MOST `Annex 2 B — the most that may be topped up in a policy year, the annualised premium at issue being` (`the request`'s `annualised regular basic premium at issue`)
    ... `the request`'s `approved by the Company`
    AND NOT (`the request`'s `during a premium holiday`)

-- Without the Policyholder's designation a top-up follows the latest allocation for the
-- regular basic premium, which it does not change.
